WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.740
How can a turkey sandwich become part of you?

2
00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:07.920
The bread came from wheat plants.

3
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:09.960
The turkey came from a bird.

4
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.380
Your body is made of cells too.

5
00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:14.380
So what are cells made of?

6
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:16.843
Think of a necklace of beads.

7
00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:21.243
A monomer is a small molecule that can join to others like it.

8
00:00:21.983 --> 00:00:25.583
A polymer is a large molecule made of many monomers in a chain.

9
00:00:26.583 --> 00:00:28.443
Real chains fold, coil and branch.

10
00:00:29.363 --> 00:00:30.783
Their shape matters for their job.

11
00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.627
How does a cell link two monomers?

12
00:00:34.387 --> 00:00:36.027
It removes a hydrogen from one.

13
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:39.647
It removes an oxygen and a hydrogen from the other.

14
00:00:40.567 --> 00:00:43.747
Overall, those atoms leave together as one water molecule.

15
00:00:44.827 --> 00:00:45.827
Joining needs energy.

16
00:00:46.647 --> 00:00:48.747
This joining is called dehydration synthesis.

17
00:00:49.707 --> 00:00:51.967
It means making something by removing water.

18
00:00:52.787 --> 00:00:54.327
The reverse is hydrolysis.

19
00:00:55.147 --> 00:00:58.307
It splits a polymer into smaller pieces by adding water.

20
00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:03.350
Scientists sort the large molecules of life into four classes.

21
00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.270
Carbohydrates are made of simple sugars.

22
00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.270
They give quick energy.

23
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:10.970
Proteins are chains of amino acids.

24
00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.110
They build tissues and run cell processes.

25
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:19.170
Nucleic acids, DNA and RNA, are chains of nucleotides.

26
00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:22.290
They store and pass on genetic information.

27
00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:25.310
Lipids mostly do not mix with water.

28
00:01:26.350 --> 00:01:30.450
Fats, built from fatty acids and glycerol, store energy for a long time.

29
00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.690
A common fat is one glycerol joined to three fatty acids.

30
00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.680
Shape decides the job, a little like a key in a lock.

31
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:44.160
Cellulose chains lie side by side in strong fibers that stiffen plant cell walls.

32
00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:50.080
An enzyme is usually a protein with a folded pocket where one kind of molecule fits.

33
00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:54.560
In DNA, two strands have bases that pair in a fixed way.

34
00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:59.420
A phospholipid has a head attracted to water and two tails that avoid it.

35
00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.280
In water, they form a double layer, heads out and tails in.

36
00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.740
That layer is the basic structure of the cell membrane.

37
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.040
So how does a sandwich become part of you?

38
00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:13.680
Digestion splits large molecules into small pieces.

39
00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:19.140
Your cells use those pieces, along with building blocks they make themselves, to

40
00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.500
build new large molecules.

41
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.420
A turkey protein does not become a human protein.

42
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.460
Its amino acids are reused in new chains.

43
00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:33.060
Four kinds of large molecule, built from a small set of building blocks, make every

44
00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.040
part of a living thing.
